{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s12CaseIterableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/SQ","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/SH","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/SY","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/13SwiftProtobuf4EnumP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For elements it selects between reviving the element already in the tree and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inserting a copy of it. The copy is what undo does today, and because a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"deep copy keeps every descendant’s created_at, it puts a second live element","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under ids the document is indexed by. Reviving needs a replicated liveness"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"register – removed_at paired with revived_at on each element – so that"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every replica resolves a remove\/revive race the same way, with a tie going","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the removal as the shipped remove register already does.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The branch cannot be chosen from local state. A replica that collected","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between the removal and the undo has purged the tombstone, and one that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joined from a later snapshot never had it, so “revive if a tombstone is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"present” is a function of local collection timing and the same change log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would produce different documents. That is why the branch is on the wire."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/yorkie\/yorkie_v1_restoremode"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode"}],"externalID":"s:6Yorkie0A15_V1_RestoreModeO","title":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Yorkie"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"RestoreMode selects the identity-preserving path. RESTORE_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means an ordinary edit (no restore semantics), keeping forward edits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unchanged on the wire."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/UNRECOGNIZED(_:)","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/restore","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/retombstone","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/unspecified"],"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/init()","doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Yorkie_V1_RestoreMode\/init(rawValue:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Yorkie\/documentation\/Yorkie\/Y